#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:5
#: 36fe60d784644ad5816513f8f254c969
msgid "Multi-Vehicle Flying"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:7
#: b6e771573f6c4d01afe14e1755cb0718
msgid "This page shows how to monitor and control multiple vehicles using a single ground station. Although this capability has been demonstrated (see video below) it is somewhat `experimental <https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/multi-vehicle-testing-with-apm-copter-tracker-and-mission-planner>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:14
#: 0410c19ea911434e8d2a390aedd164a9
msgid "This example has been greatly surpassed by `Michael Clement's 50 plane demonstration <https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/from-zero-to-fifty-planes-in-twenty-seven-minutes>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:20
#: 370da1cc78c04028900fefc7ec0e8a97
msgid "Equipment you will need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:22
#: 613dbafc4306438a8d9858c74ecb4d78
msgid "Multiple `Planes <https://ardupilot.org/plane/index.html>`_ or :ref:`Copters <copter:home>` or :ref:`Rovers <rover:home>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:25
#: b3016c7fbc5b4b578b134ea473049d76
msgid "An :ref:`Antenna Tracker <antennatracker:home>`\\ (a.k.a. Tracker) to combine the telemetry data from vehicles and send to the GCS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:27
#: 843db34ce14a41718143359a9edfdae6
msgid "Pairs of\\ :ref:`telemetry radios <common-telemetry-landingpage>` for each vehicle (i.e. 2x number of vehicles) OR multi-point radios (like the :ref:`RFD900 <common-rfd900>`) in which case just 1 radio for each vehicle + 1 for the ground station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:31
#: de788e324aa14ee2b55264fea42069b8
msgid "GCS capable of displaying/controlling multiple vehicles (i.e. the :ref:`Mission Planner <planner:home>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:33
#: dc5ed502d16549b6996f509cd5bef415
msgid "RC transmitter for each vehicle (optional)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:36
#: 8c57a3271b1142a7b3925963bf43c885
msgid "Pre-Flight Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:38
#: db526ead13144a868e1deb9c8a9dc4bf
msgid "If using SiK radios, :ref:`set the NetID <common-sik-telemetry-radio_configuring_using_the_mission_planner>` of each pair of radios to a unique number.  I.e. if controlling 3 vehicles, set the ``NetID`` of one pair to \"23\", the 2nd pair to \"24\", the 3rd pair to \"25\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:42
#: eea809b7c23e4c1cb94270c0e5aff400
msgid "Connect one of each radio pairs to the vehicle autopilots (i.e. Pixhawk) using Telem1 or Telem2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:44
#: 21e3834717ff4e01afeada17a1ac8bff
msgid "Connect the other pairs to the Tracker's controller (i.e. Pixhawk) using Telem1, Telem2 and Serial 4/5 ports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:46
#: 84051f3c88e14d209c94337ee343e80d
msgid "If using Serial 4/5 set the Tracker's ``SERIAL4_PROTOCOL`` to \"1\" to enable MAVLink communication on that port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:48
#: b2992932a96743b8973642a56b9af86d
msgid "Connect to each vehicle's autopilot and the tracker and set the ``SYSID_THISMAV`` to a unique number (i.e. \"1\" for first vehicle, \"2\" for second vehicle, \"3\" for third, \"9\" for the tracker)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:51
#: b115dc02606d46caa2b79ed4274db78c
msgid "On the GCS, :ref:`reduce data rate <planner:mission-planner-telemetry-logs-setting-the-datarate>` to the minimum acceptable value to reduce network traffic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:53
#: 9cae1a3506094a77b87c2a1712a0191b
msgid "Plug in the tracker to the ground station PC using a USB cable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:56
#: 271509d5b03248378c90a1bf7d6f5e57
msgid "Controlling the vehicles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:58
#: 5f5d819a4a784cb58f1ddd99e5257131
msgid "Plug in the battery of each vehicle and tracker.  After connecting to the tracker from the *Mission Planner* (or other GCS) each vehicle including the tracker should appear on the Map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:62
#: 713b6f384c414cb88c7cbd74052712de
msgid "Controlling the vehicle depends upon the GCS used but if using the *Mission Planner*, \"Ctrl-X\" pulls up a drop-down selector which allows the user to choose which vehicle to control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:66
#: 9f10ace32f364fe2944c4d6e9297e12f
msgid "If using Copter, switch each vehicle into GUIDED mode.  On the MP's map, right-mouse-button-click and select \"Takeoff\" and input 2m to get the vehicle off the air.  Once in the air, each vehicle can be pushed around in GUIDED mode (by using Ctrl-X to select the vehicle and then click on the map) or the mode can be changed to AUTO etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-multi-vehicle-flying.rst:72
#: 913ed7b7dced424e8e9e4a94e21fad69
msgid "If you wish to retake control of a vehicle, use the transmitter for that vehicle to change the flight to LOITER, STABILIZE, etc and then fly manually.  If only one transmitter is being used (not recommended) then use the GCS to switch the single vehicle's mode to LOITER and then control with the TX sticks (the other vehicles will ignore the TX's roll, pitch and throttle input if they are in AUTO or GUIDED - they will accept yaw input however)."
msgstr ""
